---
/**
 * How to reach the person who maintains this.
 *
 * There is no form here and there cannot be: the site is static files on a
 * CDN with no server to receive a POST, which is the same fact `/privacy/`
 * states from the other direction. So this page routes to the channels that
 * do exist and says what a useful report contains, which is the part that
 * actually decides whether a correction gets made.
 */
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { buildInfo } from "../build-info";
import { pageHref } from "../nav";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const { zigVersion } = await buildInfo();
---

<Base
  title="Contact"
  seoTitle="Contact the maintainer of Zig Guide Live"
  description="How to report an error in a chapter, suggest a topic, or reach Rajesh Pillai about this Zig guide."
  crumbs={[{ label: "Contact" }]}
  schema={{ "@type": "ContactPage", name: "Contact" }}
>
  <article>
    <h1>Contact</h1>

    <p class="lede">
      This guide is written and maintained by Rajesh Pillai. Corrections,
      questions and requests all go to the same place, and all of them are
      read.
    </p>

    <h2>Something on a page is wrong</h2>
    <p>
      This is the most useful thing you can send. Open an issue on{" "}
      <a
        href="https://github.com/rajeshpillai/zig-guide/issues"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">the issue tracker</a>. A report that can be
      acted on straight away usually has four things in it:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>The URL of the chapter.</li>
      <li>
        Your Zig version, from <code>zig version</code>. The guide targets
        master and was last verified against {zigVersion}; a good half of
        reports turn out to be a tagged release meeting code written for
        master, which is what{" "}
        <a href={pageHref("getting-started/coming-from-older-zig")}
          >coming from an older Zig</a> covers.
      </li>
      <li>What you expected to happen.</li>
      <li>What happened instead, with the error message pasted in full.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      If a snippet does not compile for you on current master, that is a build
      failure waiting to happen and worth reporting immediately. Every snippet
      is compiled and run nightly, so it should not be possible, and if it is
      happening then something about the check is wrong too. How that check
      works is written up in{" "}
      <a href={`${base}verification/`}>how this guide is verified</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>A chapter is missing, or one is unclear</h2>
    <p>
      Also the issue tracker. Say what you were trying to do and where you got
      stuck. "I could not work out how to do X" is more useful than a proposed
      table of contents, because the gap is usually somewhere other than where
      it feels like it is.
    </p>

    <h2>A correction you have already written</h2>
    <p>
      Pull requests are welcome at{" "}
      <a
        href="https://github.com/rajeshpillai/zig-guide"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">github.com/rajeshpillai/zig-guide</a>. Every
      snippet is a real file that the build compiles and runs, so a change to
      example code is checked automatically the moment it is pushed. The
      repository's own notes describe how snippets are classified and what a new
      one needs.
    </p>

    <h2>Anything else</h2>
    <p>
      Rajesh is on X as{" "}
      <a href="https://twitter.com/rajeshpillai" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >@rajeshpillai</a>, and reachable through the same GitHub account for
      anything that does not belong in a public issue.
    </p>

    <h2>What this site cannot do</h2>
    <p>
      It has no accounts, no comment system and no server. Nothing here can
      receive a form submission, store a message, or email you back, which is
      why every route above leaves this domain. The same fact is why there is so
      little to say on <a href={`${base}privacy/`}>privacy</a>.
    </p>

    <p><a href={`${base}about/`}>About this guide →</a></p>
  </article>
</Base>
